        <mxCell id="legend-stack-7-text" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;2 replicas&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="362" y="2702" width="188" height="22" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-legend-notes" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;Large dashed frame: infra perimeter · small: functional group&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;⚠ Gx&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: docs and code disagree, see &quot;Gaps&quot;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="2770" width="480" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-status" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#d97706&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Where things stand&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Admin hub&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: Argo CD and Vault stay on-prem, alone. Today the hub and the onprem target are the same K3s cluster, registered twice in Argo CD (in-cluster and onprem).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;onprem&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; is the only registered target: tested end to end. &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;cloud-a&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: the aws and gcp cluster secrets exist, left out of Argo CD until their Vault path is filled.&lt;br&gt;• A project lives on one cloud: its record in cnp-projects carries &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;target_cloud&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;, and all its apps, prod and staging, go there. Two clouds, two projects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; to &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;: user traffic enters through the project&amp;#39;s own tunnel and gateway on its cluster, never through the hub (invariant I-1). &amp;lt;app-b&amp;gt; and &amp;lt;project-b&amp;gt; follow the same path, unnumbered.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; Argo CD syncs each target, &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;D&lt;/span&gt; each secret operator reads Vault. Only &amp;lt;cloud-a&amp;gt; crosses the VPN, best effort. If the hub is down, running apps keep serving and logging users in.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="2520" width="860" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-gaps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ea580c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Gaps between the plan and the code&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G14&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Per-project edge.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Gateway, tunnel and Keycloak IAMaaS are in cnp-project-base, off by default: live projects still use the hub&amp;#39;s shared gateway and tunnel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G11&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Vault auth.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; One Kubernetes auth mount for every cluster (D-07 not built).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G12&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Storage class.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; local-path is hardcoded; no per-cloud profile (D-08).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G13&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Secret operator.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; The Ricoberger operator, not HashiCorp VSO: whether a synced Secret survives a Vault outage is untested (GD-1).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G3&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Transport.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; TLS ends at Cloudflare; behind the tunnel, hops are plain HTTP.&lt;br&gt;• vmagent per cluster and the blackbox probes (D-10) are not started.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1480" y="2520" width="780" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
